ight retained by author; no open license verified ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (12 October 2026)\n"},{"id":"japan-adv-amami-iriomote","title":"L’inscription naturelle du sud-ouest couvre-t-elle toutes les îles d’Okinawa ?","domain":"geography","level":"culture","aliases":["Amami","Tokunoshima","Okinawa","Iriomote","subtropical"],"explanationFr":"Le bien inscrit réunit des zones forestières d’Amami-Ōshima, Tokunoshima, du nord de l’île d’Okinawa et d’Iriomote. Il ne désigne pas l’ensemble des territoires habités de ces îles. Les forêts pluviales subtropicales abritent une forte proportion d’espèces endémiques, dont certaines sont propres à une seule île du groupe.","scopeNote":"La délimitation d’un bien naturel ne doit pas être confondue avec une frontière administrative ou la totalité d’un archipel.","prerequisites":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1574/","title":"Amami-Oshima, Tokunoshima, Northern Okinawa and Iriomote","publisher":"UNESCO World Heritage Centre","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","availability":"consulted","license":"Property descriptions display CC-BY-SA IGO 3.0. Photographs, maps and nomination files have separate rights.","reuse":"Original factual synthesis and attribution; no copied description, image, map or audio."}],"backlogRefs":["japan-backlog-geography-03","japan-backlog-society-07"],"status":"source-reviewed-draft","claimType":"fact","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","reviewState":{"sourceClaim":"checked","japaneseExample":"not-applicable","nativeReview":"pending"},"examples":[],"levelEstimated":false,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/japan/JapanAdvancedRecords.json","corpus":"japan","recordShard":100,"markdown":"## japan-adv-amami-iriomote : L’inscription naturelle du sud-ouest couvre-t-elle toutes les îles d’Okinawa ? (12 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : geography ; niveau : culture ; statut : source-reviewed-draft. (12 October 2026)\n\nLe bien inscrit réunit des zones forestières d’Amami-Ōshima, Tokunoshima, du nord de l’île d’Okinawa et d’Iriomote. Il ne désigne pas l’ensemble des territoires habités de ces îles. Les forêts pluviales subtropicales abritent une forte proportion d’espèces endémiques, dont certaines sont propres à une seule île du groupe. (12 October 2026)\n\n- [Amami-Oshima, Tokunoshima, Northern Okinawa and Iriomote](https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1574/) ; UNESCO World Heritage Centre ; Property descriptions display CC-BY-SA IGO 3.0. Photographs, maps and nomination files have separate rights. ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (12 October 2026)\n"},{"id":"word-1006670","title":"其処","aliases":["其処","其所","そこ"],"domain":"dictionary","level":"unclassified","levelEstimated":false,"status":"source-imported","explanationFr":"EN : there (place relatively near listener) [pronoun, word usually written using kana alone]\n\nEN : there (place just mentioned); EN : that place [pronoun, word usually written using kana alone]\n\nEN : then (of some incident just spoken of); EN : that (of point just raised) [pronoun, word usually written using kana alone]\n\nEN : you [pronoun, archaic]\n\nFR : là (lieu relativement proche de l'auditeur) [pronoun]\n\nFR : là (lieu qui vient d'être cité); FR : cet endroit [pronoun]\n\nFR : alors (à propos d'un incident dont on vient de parler); FR : cela (à propos d'un point que l'on vient d'évoquer) [pronoun]\n\nFR : vous [pronoun]","glossLanguages":["eng","fre"],"senses":[{"partOfSpeech":["pn"],"appliesToKanji":["*"],"appliesToKana":["*"],"related":[["どこ",1],["ここ",1],["あそこ",1]],"antonym":[],"field":[],"dialect":[],"misc":["uk"],"info":[],"languageSource":[],"gloss":[{"lang":"eng","gender":null,"type":null,"text":"there (place relatively near listener)"}]},{"partOfSpeech":["pn"],"appliesToKanji":["*"],"appliesToKana":["*"],"related":[],"antonym":[],"field":[],"dialect":[],"misc":["uk"],"info":[],"languageSource":[],"gloss":[{"lang":"eng","gender":null,"type":null,"text":"there (place just mentioned)"},{"lang":"eng","gender":null,"typ